requirements.oracle:
A protected header JSON object reformatted with inserted spaces, tabs and newlines between members (e.g. "{
  "alg" : "HS256" ,
  "typ":"JWT"
}
"), base64url-encoded and fed to header.Header.Unmarshal, decodes to the same Algorithm/Type as the compact form. Likewise a full JWS JSON Serialization envelope reformatted with indentation decodes via json.Unmarshal into *jwt.Token identically to its compact-printed counterpart. Verified empirically: Go's encoding/json already tolerates exactly this whitespace by default, so the library adds no extra restriction beyond RFC 7159.
